========================================================================
  H-WEIGHTED INDEPENDENCE POLYNOMIAL
========================================================================

  Define I_H(G_n, x) = sum over independent sets S of
  x^|S| * prod_{i in S} H(class_i).

  This weights each independent set by the product of H values.

  n=3: I_H(G_3, x) = 1 + 4*x
    I_H(G_3, 1) = 5
    I_H(G_3, 2) = 9

  n=4: I_H(G_4, x) = 1 + 12*x + 9*x^2
    I_H(G_4, 1) = 22
    I_H(G_4, 2) = 61

  n=5: I_H(G_5, x) = 1 + 92*x + 1906*x^2 + 13056*x^3 + 26010*x^4 + 6804*x^5
    I_H(G_5, 1) = 47869
    I_H(G_5, 2) = 746145


========================================================================
  SIZE-WEIGHTED INDEPENDENCE POLYNOMIAL
========================================================================

  I_S(G_n, x) = sum over independent sets S of
  x^|S| * prod_{i in S} size(class_i).

  Weights by how many labeled tournaments each class represents.

  n=3: I_S(G_3, x) = 1 + 8*x
    I_S(G_3, 1) = 9
    I_S(G_3, 2) = 17
    2^C(n,2) = 8

  n=4: I_S(G_4, x) = 1 + 64*x + 64*x^2
    I_S(G_4, 1) = 129
    I_S(G_4, 2) = 385
    2^C(n,2) = 64

  n=5: I_S(G_5, x) = 1 + 1024*x + 179840*x^2 + 8115200*x^3 + 153600000*x^4 + 1105920000*x^5
    I_S(G_5, 1) = 1267816065
    I_S(G_5, 2) = 37912683009
    2^C(n,2) = 1024


========================================================================
  CLIQUE POLYNOMIAL OF G_n
========================================================================

  C(G_n, x) = sum over cliques S of x^|S|.
  This = I(complement(G_n), x).

  n=3: C(G_3, x) = 1 + 2*x + x^2
    C(G_3, 1) = 4 (total cliques)
    C(G_3, 2) = 9
    Clique number omega(G_3) = 2

  n=4: C(G_4, x) = 1 + 4*x + 5*x^2 + 2*x^3
    C(G_4, 1) = 12 (total cliques)
    C(G_4, 2) = 45
    Clique number omega(G_4) = 3

  n=5: C(G_5, x) = 1 + 12*x + 30*x^2 + 21*x^3 + 4*x^4
    C(G_5, 1) = 68 (total cliques)
    C(G_5, 2) = 377
    Clique number omega(G_5) = 4


========================================================================
  MATCHING POLYNOMIAL OF G_n
========================================================================

  mu(G_n, x) = sum_k (-1)^k * m_k * x^{|V|-2k}
  where m_k = number of k-matchings (k independent edges).

  n=3: matching numbers m_k = [1, 1]
    Maximum matching size = 1
    Total matchings = 2

  n=4: matching numbers m_k = [1, 5, 2]
    Maximum matching size = 2
    Total matchings = 8

  n=5: matching numbers m_k = [1, 30, 296, 1163, 1760, 821, 55]
    Maximum matching size = 6
    Total matchings = 4126


========================================================================
  THE DEEP CONNECTION
========================================================================


THE SELF-REFERENTIAL STRUCTURE:

Level 0: A tournament T on n vertices.
Level 1: Its conflict graph Omega(T) — vertices are odd cycles,
         edges are shared-vertex conflicts.
Level 2: H(T) = I(Omega(T), 2) — the OCF.
Level 3: G_n — the graph whose vertices are tournament iso classes,
         edges are single-arc reversals.
Level 4: I(G_n, x) — the independence polynomial of the class graph.

I(G_n, 2) counts something about tournament classes:
the number of ways to choose independent sets of classes
(classes no two of which are connected by a single arc reversal)
weighted by 2^k.

WHAT DOES AN INDEPENDENT SET IN G_n MEAN?

An independent set S in G_n is a collection of tournament iso classes
such that NO single arc reversal connects any two classes in S.
These classes are "isolated from each other" — you need at least
TWO arc reversals to get from any class in S to any other class in S.

I(G_n, 2) counts these isolated collections with weight 2^|S|.

  n=3:
    I(G_3, x) = 1 + 2*x
    I(G_3, 2) = 5
    Maximum independent sets (alpha=1):
      classes [0] with H = [1]
      classes [1] with H = [3]

  n=4:
    I(G_4, x) = 1 + 4*x + x^2
    I(G_4, 2) = 13
    Maximum independent sets (alpha=2):
      classes [1, 3] with H = [3, 3]

  n=5:
    I(G_5, x) = 1 + 12*x + 36*x^2 + 38*x^3 + 16*x^4 + 2*x^5
    I(G_5, 2) = 793
    Maximum independent sets (alpha=5):
      classes [1, 3, 4, 7, 10] with H = [3, 3, 9, 3, 13]
      classes [1, 3, 4, 7, 11] with H = [3, 3, 9, 3, 15]


