  FACTORIZATION OF I(G_n, x)
========================================================================

  n=3: I(G_3, x) = 1 + 2*x
    I(G_3, -1) = -1

  n=4: I(G_4, x) = 1 + 4*x + x^2
    I(G_4, -1) = -2
    Real roots: [-3.7321, -0.2679]
    All roots real and negative: True
    => G_4 is likely claw-free!

  n=5: I(G_5, x) = 1 + 12*x + 36*x^2 + 38*x^3 + 16*x^4 + 2*x^5
    I(G_5, -1) = 1
    Real roots: [-4.7342, -0.4328, -0.1233]
    Complex roots: [(-1.3548, 0.3786), (-1.3548, -0.3786)]
    All roots real and negative: False


========================================================================
  COMPARING I(G_n, x) WITH I(Omega, x)
========================================================================

  For each tournament class, I(Omega(T), x) is the independence
  polynomial of its conflict graph. H(T) = I(Omega(T), 2).

  n=3:
    class 0: H=1, I(Omega, x) = 1 + 0*x, I(Omega, 2) = 1
    class 1: H=3, I(Omega, x) = 1 + 1*x, I(Omega, 2) = 3

  n=4:
    class 0: H=1, I(Omega, x) = 1 + 0*x, I(Omega, 2) = 1
    class 1: H=3, I(Omega, x) = 1 + 1*x, I(Omega, 2) = 3
    class 2: H=5, I(Omega, x) = 1 + 2*x, I(Omega, 2) = 5
    class 3: H=3, I(Omega, x) = 1 + 1*x, I(Omega, 2) = 3

  n=5:
    class 0: H=1, I(Omega, x) = 1 + 0*x, I(Omega, 2) = 1
    class 1: H=3, I(Omega, x) = 1 + 1*x, I(Omega, 2) = 3
    class 2: H=5, I(Omega, x) = 1 + 2*x, I(Omega, 2) = 5
    class 3: H=3, I(Omega, x) = 1 + 1*x, I(Omega, 2) = 3
    class 4: H=9, I(Omega, x) = 1 + 4*x, I(Omega, 2) = 9
    class 5: H=5, I(Omega, x) = 1 + 2*x, I(Omega, 2) = 5
    class 6: H=9, I(Omega, x) = 1 + 4*x, I(Omega, 2) = 9
    class 7: H=3, I(Omega, x) = 1 + 1*x, I(Omega, 2) = 3
    class 8: H=11, I(Omega, x) = 1 + 5*x, I(Omega, 2) = 11
    class 9: H=15, I(Omega, x) = 1 + 7*x, I(Omega, 2) = 15
    class 10: H=13, I(Omega, x) = 1 + 6*x, I(Omega, 2) = 13
    class 11: H=15, I(Omega, x) = 1 + 7*x, I(Omega, 2) = 15


